/* In the flow, in the leading slot of whatever bar the screen has. Never fixed.
 *
 * It WAS `position: fixed` in the viewport corner, and that is exactly what put
 * it under the page header: the header is `position: sticky` with an opaque
 * background at the same `--z-sticky` level, so at equal z-index the later
 * element in the DOM wins and painted over the top half of the button. A
 * floating control and an opaque bar were competing for the same corner, and no
 * z-index fixes that — one of them has to not be there.
 *
 * Above the drawer breakpoint the sidebar is on screen and the button has
 * nothing to do, so it is not rendered at all. */
.nav-drawer-button { display: none; }

@media (max-width: 48rem) {
  .nav-drawer-button { display: inline-flex; }
}
